WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:01.339
Water.

00:00:01.339 --> 00:00:03.310
The wellspring of life.

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:09.280
We’ve dealt with a number of anomalous water
sources on this channel, like SCP-006, the

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:15.350
much sought-after Fountain of Youth, or the
terrifying SCP-3280, where murderous water

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.820
threatens to destroy the entire world.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:22.949
But we’ve never seen anomalous water that
behaves quite like this before...

00:00:22.949 --> 00:00:27.999
In many of the legends of King Arthur, the
sword of Excalibur is presented to him by

00:00:27.999 --> 00:00:30.339
the mystical Lady of the Lake.

00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:35.600
This lady emerges from the depths of the water,
gifting Arthur with the enchanted sword.

00:00:35.600 --> 00:00:41.670
It’s an incredible, if impossible, image:
a woman appearing from within the lake, rising

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.390
up from the bottom and breaking through the
surface.

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:48.710
It’s safe to say that none of us have ever
seen anything quite like it.

00:00:48.710 --> 00:00:51.210
Well, at least most of us haven’t.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:56.100
In a small unnamed English village, there
was a young woman who set out on a particularly

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:59.970
lovely, warm Spring day to take a swim in
a nearby lake.

00:00:59.970 --> 00:01:04.930
While wading in the water, enjoying the sunlight
and the gentle breeze on her skin, she saw

00:01:04.930 --> 00:01:08.049
a strange ripple ghost across the surface.

00:01:08.049 --> 00:01:10.950
She stopped her swimming, staring at the motion.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:14.770
She expected to spot a fish or some other
aquatic creature.

00:01:14.770 --> 00:01:20.560
Instead, the water itself began to rise up,
gathering and forming into a shape before

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:21.770
her eyes.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:26.229
It was impossible, and yet here it was, happening.

00:01:26.229 --> 00:01:30.729
She pinched herself and found that she was
definitely awake, as the water transformed

00:01:30.729 --> 00:01:33.060
into the shape of a human woman.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:37.590
It turned to look at her, shimmering eyes
finding hers and liquid lips forming into

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:39.900
a warm, inviting smile.

00:01:39.900 --> 00:01:44.130
Though this being was shocking to see, it
clearly meant her no harm.

00:01:44.130 --> 00:01:50.070
It raised a translucent arm and gave her a
small wave as if to welcome her to its home.

00:01:50.070 --> 00:01:54.139
The young woman approached this Lady of the
Lake, reaching out her own hand of flesh and

00:01:54.139 --> 00:01:57.490
bone to touch this impossible creature.

00:01:57.490 --> 00:02:02.049
Just as her fingertips reached the water woman’s
own, the figure dissolved back into the lake

00:02:02.049 --> 00:02:03.350
with a splash.

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:07.600
The young woman ran back home, telling anyone
who would listen about the incredible thing

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.590
she had seen that day.

00:02:09.590 --> 00:02:11.439
Of course, no one believed her.

00:02:11.439 --> 00:02:16.720
That is, until word of her sighting reached
the only people who might take her claim seriously:

00:02:16.720 --> 00:02:18.930
The SCP Foundation.

00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:22.989
They sent operatives to the lake, where they
managed to capture the shapeshifting entity

00:02:22.989 --> 00:02:24.840
dwelling there.

00:02:24.840 --> 00:02:30.210
SCP-054, also known as “The Water Nymph”,
is a being made up entirely of water, with

00:02:30.210 --> 00:02:32.459
an average volume of 90 liters.

00:02:32.459 --> 00:02:36.989
When it is out of a body of water, the being
tends to adopt the appearance of a humanoid

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:42.220
woman, though it is capable of taking on a
variety of other shapes including other humanoids,

00:02:42.220 --> 00:02:45.150
animals, and various inanimate objects.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:49.490
The entity is also capable of shedding its
form and effectively disappearing into a given

00:02:49.490 --> 00:02:50.829
body of water.

00:02:50.829 --> 00:02:57.640
In order to avoid shrinking, or possibly disappearing
entirely, from evaporation, SCP-054 is required

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.519
to return to a larger body of water.

00:03:00.519 --> 00:03:05.049
Studies of samples taken from the entity’s
body, or its version of a body, revealed that

00:03:05.049 --> 00:03:07.230
it is made up of ordinary water.

00:03:07.230 --> 00:03:12.420
There is no apparent reason for its ability
to move, and no thermal, electromagnetic,

00:03:12.420 --> 00:03:15.019
biological, or supernatural anomalies were
detected.

00:03:15.019 --> 00:03:20.129
The research team could not determine what
might make this water alive and sentient,

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:24.430
and the nature of its unusual properties is
uncertain to this day.

00:03:24.430 --> 00:03:30.620
When SCP-054 was first brought into containment
at Site-08, it displayed surprisingly congenial

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:35.580
and curious behavior, often walking around
outside of the water and taking turns mimicking

00:03:35.580 --> 00:03:39.130
the shapes of various staff and scientists
that spoke to it.

00:03:39.130 --> 00:03:43.470
Its demeanor began to shift toward suspicion
and aggression, however, following a series

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:47.400
of experiments and an incident involving the
research staff.

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:52.189
The first experiment conducted on SCP-054
sought to determine what would happen if the

00:03:52.189 --> 00:03:54.960
entity was denied access to any freshwater.

00:03:54.960 --> 00:03:58.670
Water was drained from the fountain holding
it, leaving only enough water for it to form

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:03.079
a humanoid shape, but no additional water
in the basin to compensate for the effects

00:04:03.079 --> 00:04:05.689
of evaporation over time.

00:04:05.689 --> 00:04:10.810
SCP-054 became visibly frustrated as the water
was being drained out of its enclosure.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:14.810
For the next few days, it enthusiastically
greeted anyone who entered its containment

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:19.360
facility, attempting to use a rapport and
sense of familiarity to convince the person

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:21.470
to provide it with more water.

00:04:21.470 --> 00:04:25.400
After it realized that this approach had no
impact on the amount of water in its fountain,

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:29.830
it became distant and even cold to anyone
who attempted to speak to it.

00:04:29.830 --> 00:04:35.419
054 only became friendly again once the water
in its fountain was restored to a pre-experiment

00:04:35.419 --> 00:04:36.419
level.

00:04:36.419 --> 00:04:42.280
Next, the research team opted to test SCP-054’s
reaction to extreme temperatures, particularly

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:43.790
extreme cold.

00:04:43.790 --> 00:04:47.700
The temperature of the containment facility
was slowly dropped until the room fell below

00:04:47.700 --> 00:04:49.680
the freezing point of water.

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:53.550
As the temperature dropped, 054 became sluggish
and exhausted.

00:04:53.550 --> 00:04:58.960
It lost its ability to shift between forms,
remaining locked in its preferred humanoid

00:04:58.960 --> 00:05:00.419
female shape.

00:05:00.419 --> 00:05:05.030
Its movements slowed more and more as the
room grew colder, until the entity was completely

00:05:05.030 --> 00:05:06.430
frozen solid.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:10.160
Portions of the ice were chipped off and studied,
revealing that the crystals were identical

00:05:10.160 --> 00:05:12.699
to those of any ordinary ice.

00:05:12.699 --> 00:05:16.919
After the sub-zero testing, the research team
decided to take things to the other end of

00:05:16.919 --> 00:05:21.510
the spectrum and test the effects of heat
on SCP-054.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:25.610
The subject was placed in a tank outfitted
with heating equipment, and its temperature

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:28.160
was slowly raised over the course of several
minutes.

00:05:28.160 --> 00:05:33.050
When the water reached a temperature of 95
degrees, the entity’s behavior became frenetic

00:05:33.050 --> 00:05:34.050
and aggressive.

00:05:34.050 --> 00:05:38.060
It pounded on the glass walls of the tank
and attempted to break through the lid in

00:05:38.060 --> 00:05:43.060
a desperate bid for escape until the temperature
was returned to a comfortable level.

00:05:43.060 --> 00:05:46.919
After the extreme temperature experiments,
the previously calm and cooperative nature

00:05:46.919 --> 00:05:50.280
of SCP-054 was nowhere to be found.

00:05:50.280 --> 00:05:54.380
The subject displayed increased suspicion
of the research team, and would fight back

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:58.870
whenever it was removed from its fountain
and taken to a lab for experimentation.

00:05:58.870 --> 00:06:03.150
In spite of this newfound resistance, the
team decided to continue their experiments

00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:08.450
as planned, hoping that the entity would return
to its formerly docile self over time.

00:06:08.450 --> 00:06:14.240
Next, Dr. Seskel, the acting head of the research
team, conducted a study involving SCP 054’s

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:16.900
memory and ability to be conditioned.

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:21.910
The entity was presented with a series of
increasingly complex mazes and puzzles.

00:06:21.910 --> 00:06:26.220
When it failed to comply with the experiment,
or solved a puzzle incorrectly, the entity

00:06:26.220 --> 00:06:31.170
was punished with an electrical shock or the
release of silica gel into its body.

00:06:31.170 --> 00:06:35.479
Both of these options seemed to cause it a
great deal of pain and distress, and it was

00:06:35.479 --> 00:06:38.710
eager to avoid further exposure to them.

00:06:38.710 --> 00:06:43.440
SCP-054 displayed impressive learning and
problem-solving capabilities, revealing it

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:46.880
is likely much more intelligent than it was
first presumed to be.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:51.690
Dr. Seskel, observing the experiments and
with the effectiveness of his somewhat unsavory

00:06:51.690 --> 00:06:56.099
motivational techniques, quipped to his research
assistant that they would “have it trained

00:06:56.099 --> 00:06:57.990
to fetch in no time.”

00:06:57.990 --> 00:07:02.530
After several days of these experiments, and
repeated use of both the silica gel and electrical

00:07:02.530 --> 00:07:08.060
shocks, the entity’s progress slowed down
considerably and it became visibly exhausted.

00:07:08.060 --> 00:07:13.000
It was removed from the lab for a 48 hour
rest period, before experimentation was resumed

00:07:13.000 --> 00:07:14.180
yet again.

00:07:14.180 --> 00:07:20.430
This time, Dr. Seskel planned to expose SCP-054’s
water source to various levels of acids and

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:26.790
bases in order to test its homeostatic capabilities,
beginning with a 0.5 M solution of hydrochloric

00:07:26.790 --> 00:07:27.790
acid.

00:07:27.790 --> 00:07:33.039
Prior to conducting the experiment, Dr. Seskel
noted: “I have no idea what will happen,

00:07:33.039 --> 00:07:38.060
but if this thing incorporates homeostatic
mechanisms like I suspect then we should get

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:41.120
some insight into how it maintains its form.”

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:46.080
He also noted that SCP-054’s behavior was
becoming “increasingly erratic,” but made

00:07:46.080 --> 00:07:49.629
the decision to continue with the experiment
as planned.

00:07:49.629 --> 00:07:54.260
SCP-054 displayed a now-familiar reluctance
when it was removed from its containment chamber

00:07:54.260 --> 00:07:55.960
and taken to the lab.

00:07:55.960 --> 00:08:00.169
It thrashed around in the fountain, splashing
researchers with water and retreating from

00:08:00.169 --> 00:08:01.629
them as they approached.

00:08:01.629 --> 00:08:06.520
In spite of its efforts, however, it was removed
from its fountain and placed in the experimental

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:07.520
tank.

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:12.300
The solution of hydrochloric acid was then
dripped into the tank, and then all hell broke

00:08:12.300 --> 00:08:13.300
loose.

00:08:13.300 --> 00:08:18.900
As soon as the acid touched the surface of
its water, SCP-054 became incredibly distressed.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:23.810
It formed into the shape of a human face,
eyes wide, mouth open in a silent scream of

00:08:23.810 --> 00:08:25.379
rage and pain.

00:08:25.379 --> 00:08:29.470
The water churned so aggressively that the
lid of the tank was shaken loose, allowing

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:32.070
it to escape the boundaries of its containment.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:36.200
The water formed into two large hands, which
shot out from the tank and grabbed the two

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:40.820
nearest researchers, pulling them into the
water and exposing their skin to the acid

00:08:40.820 --> 00:08:42.330
now present there.

00:08:42.330 --> 00:08:45.620
As the men scrambled to drag themselves back
out of the tank, and their colleagues were

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:51.529
busy helping them, SCP-054 took on its usual
humanoid form and ran for the door.

00:08:51.529 --> 00:08:55.560
It then collapsed into a puddle, slipped under
the crack in the bottom of the door, and made

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:57.110
its way down the hall.

00:08:57.110 --> 00:09:01.430
It was apprehended roughly ten minutes after
its escape by a team of guards, who froze

00:09:01.430 --> 00:09:06.360
it using canisters of liquid nitrogen and
then carried its icy body back to the containment

00:09:06.360 --> 00:09:07.360
facility.

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:11.240
The two researchers who had been pulled into
the tank experienced chemical burns on their

00:09:11.240 --> 00:09:14.760
skin, as well as significant mental distress.

00:09:14.760 --> 00:09:19.200
They were given immediate medical attention
and placed on a leave of absence, and all

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:23.880
experimentation on SCP-054 was suspended until
further notice.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:29.720
At the recommendation of Dr. Seskal, 054’s
object class was changed to “Euclid.”

00:09:29.720 --> 00:09:35.250
SCP-054 is currently contained in a watertight
isolation room, fitted with climate control

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:36.250
equipment.

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:40.140
A beautiful, intricately designed fountain
has been placed in the center of the containment

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:44.800
room, filled with fresh spring water in order
to accommodate the entity’s environmental

00:09:44.800 --> 00:09:45.800
needs.

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:50.360
All maintenance workers assigned to the area
must wear NBC suits while inside and must

00:09:50.360 --> 00:09:54.519
spend ten minutes isolated in a drying room
after exiting before they are permitted to

00:09:54.519 --> 00:09:56.480
return to the rest of the facility.

00:09:56.480 --> 00:10:01.980
If 054 breaches containment, the area must
be evacuated and the containment chamber will

00:10:01.980 --> 00:10:05.820
be filled with liquid nitrogen in order to
freeze its water solid.

00:10:05.820 --> 00:10:10.320
As the entity is highly sensitive to the conditions
of the water that houses it, chemical levels

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:14.880
and volume of the water in the fountain must
be monitored on a regular basis, and kept

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:18.450
at optimal levels for the health of SCP-054.

00:10:18.450 --> 00:10:23.140
During the course of its containment following
the incident around the acid/base incorporation

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:28.680
experiment, 054 has developed a distrust of
men, as the researchers handling that experiment

00:10:28.680 --> 00:10:30.540
were primarily male.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:36.660
In order to prevent future incidents and keep
SCP-054 calm, no male staff are to be assigned

00:10:36.660 --> 00:10:39.700
to the team monitoring its containment unit.

00:10:39.700 --> 00:10:44.880
Because five years have passed since the last
incident involving SCP-054, its object class

00:10:44.880 --> 00:10:49.029
has been changed from “Euclid” to “Safe”
on the recommendation of the lead researcher

00:10:49.029 --> 00:10:50.620
assigned to its case.

00:10:50.620 --> 00:10:54.990
Of course, caution should still be exercised
while interacting with the entity.

00:10:54.990 --> 00:10:59.430
This is the SCP Foundation, after all, and
just because a moderate amount of water is

00:10:59.430 --> 00:11:03.380
good for you, doesn’t mean you can’t still
drown.

00:11:03.380 --> 00:11:08.050
Experimentation on SCP-054 has resumed, though
this time its boundaries are being honored

00:11:08.050 --> 00:11:12.279
and it is allowed adequate time to rest and
recuperate between experiments.

00:11:12.279 --> 00:11:16.880
All use of punishment in order to motivate
the entity has been suspended, as it has shown

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.130
itself to be more than willing to cooperate
if it is treated with respect.

00:11:21.130 --> 00:11:26.600
Like all of us, it responds far better to
kindness than it does to fear and intimidation.

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:31.220
It doesn’t just take on the appearance of
a person, it has thoughts, feelings, and the

00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:33.649
urge to defend itself when threatened.

00:11:33.649 --> 00:11:37.670
So think twice next time you find yourself
swimming in a random body of water.

00:11:37.670 --> 00:11:40.529
You should be mindful of what might be living
in there.

00:11:40.529 --> 00:11:46.290
Not just of the fish, the algae, and the tiny
water bugs, but of the invisible, intelligent,

00:11:46.290 --> 00:11:50.899
impossible creatures that might be swimming
in there with you, or even make up the very

00:11:50.899 --> 00:11:52.480
water itself.

00:11:52.480 --> 00:11:58.170
Now go check out “SCP-173 - The Sculpture”
and “SCP-682 - The Hard to Kill Reptile”

00:11:58.170 --> 00:12:01.230
for more enigmatic entities of the SCP Foundation!

